{"id":"11C","title":"Alliances and Treaties","part":{"n":11,"title":"Foreign relations"},"url":"/law/11-foreign-relations/11c","entries":[{"id":"11C.1","text":"Alliances and covenants (treaties) with pagan or ungodly nations are forbidden.","refs":[{"book":"Exodus","chapter":23,"verses":"32"},{"book":"Exodus","chapter":34,"verses":"12-16"},{"book":"Deuteronomy","chapter":7,"verses":"2-4"},{"book":"Judges","chapter":2,"verses":"2-3"},{"book":"Ezra","chapter":9,"verses":"12"},{"book":"Psalms","chapter":106,"verses":"34-36"}],"citation":"Exod. 23:32; Exod. 34:12-16; Deut. 7:2-4; Judges 2:2-3; Ezra 9:12; Psa. 106:34-36."},{"id":"11C.2","text":"Covenants with pagan or ungodly nations leads to idolatry and adoption of pagan ways.","refs":[{"book":"Exodus","chapter":34,"verses":"12-16"},{"book":"Deuteronomy","chapter":7,"verses":"2-4"}],"citation":"Exod. 34:12-16; Deut. 7:2-4."},{"id":"11C.3","text":"Do not to follow the ways of other nations.","refs":[{"book":"Deuteronomy","chapter":12,"verses":"29-30"}],"citation":"Deut. 12:29-30."},{"id":"11C.4","text":"A treaty of peace, agreeing to do no harm to another friendly nation, can be enacted.","refs":[{"book":"Genesis","chapter":21,"verses":"22-32"},{"book":"Genesis","chapter":26,"verses":"28-31"}],"citation":"Gen. 21:22-32; Gen. 26:28-31."},{"id":"11C.5","text":"Alliances made with wicked nations will not be fruitful.","refs":[{"book":"2 Chronicles","chapter":20,"verses":"35-37"}],"citation":"2 Chron. 20:35-37."}]}